This directory contains QuIDDPro scripts which simulate some of the
sample circuits bundled with Scott Aaronson's CHP stabilizer circuit
simulator (http://www.cs.berkeley.edu/~aaronson/chp.html).  A program
to convert CHP circuits to QuIDDPro scripts is also included.

The conversion program is called "quidd_convert."  It takes two
command-line arguments.  The first argument is the name and path of
the CHP stabilizer circuit to convert.  The second argument is the
number of qubits in the stabilizer circuit.  The QuIDDPro script is
simply sent to standard out.  So, to store the generated QuIDDPro
script to a file, redirect standard out to a file.  For example,

./quidd_convert epr.chp 2 > epr.qpro

will convert the CHP stabilizer circuit "epr.chp" to a QuIDDPro script
and save it as "epr.qpro."

Scripts
-------

epr.qpro: A 2-qubit simulation of an EPR pair.

qecc9.qpro: A single qubit encoded with Shor's code.

chp100.qpro: A 100-qubit circuit with 300 randomly generated
	      stabilizer gates.
